# Figma MCP Workflow

## When a Figma link is pasted

1. Use Figma MCP to inspect the node.
2. Extract in order: name, variants/properties, nested components, auto-layout, styles (color, typography, spacing).
3. Map every Figma style value to a token:
   - Color → nearest `tokens.*` semantic token
   - Font style → `TypographyVariant` from `@theme/typography.ts`
   - Spacing → nearest `spacing.*` value from `@theme/spacing.ts`
4. Before building: summarize what you found and ask the user to confirm.

## Figma Layer Naming Conventions

Layers in Figma follow this naming convention (agreed with Bukovel design team):
- Component names: PascalCase — `AppButton`, `AppInput`
- Variants property: `Variant` — values: `primary`, `secondary`, `ghost`, `destructive`
- Size property: `Size` — values: `small`, `medium`, `large`
- State property: `State` — values: `default`, `pressed`, `disabled`, `loading`, `error`, `focus`
- Boolean props: `Is` prefix — `IsDisabled`, `IsLoading`, `HasIcon`

When Figma properties use different names, map them to the above convention in code and flag the discrepancy.

## Token Mapping Rules

### Colors
Check Figma fill/stroke → find matching semantic token.
If no match exists:
- Check if the raw hex matches a primitive → ask which semantic token it should map to
- Never silently introduce a new hardcoded color

Priority order for color token matching:
1. Exact token match by role (e.g. button background → `tokens.intPrimary`)
2. Nearest primitive value
3. Flag as unmapped and ask

### Typography
Figma text style name → `TypographyVariant`:
```
body-1             → body1
body-1-highlight   → body1Highlight
body-1-tiny        → body1Tiny
title-1            → title1
caption-regular    → captionRegular
caption-label      → captionLabel
cta-large          → ctaLarge
display-1          → display1
```
If Figma uses a style not in this list → flag it: "Figma uses '[name]' which has no matching token. Closest: '[nearest]'. Use that, or add a new variant?"

### Spacing
Round Figma spacing values to nearest 4px grid value:
```
1-2px   → spacing.tiny (4)
5-10px  → spacing.small (8)
11-14px → spacing.medium (12)
15-18px → spacing.large (16)
19-22px → spacing.extraLarge (20)
23-26px → spacing.xxLarge (24)
27-36px → spacing.xxxLarge (32)
37-44px → spacing.xxxxLarge (40)
```
If off-grid by more than 2px, flag it: "Figma has [X]px here which is off the 4px grid. Rounding to [nearest]. Ok?"

## Component Type Detection

Read the Figma layer hierarchy to determine atomic category:

- **Atom**: single node or composed of only primitives (Text, Icon, Shape)
  → `src/components/atoms/`

- **Molecule**: contains 2+ atom-level components
  → `src/components/molecules/`

- **Organism**: contains molecules or is a full screen section
  → `src/components/organisms/`

When uncertain, ask.

## After Every Build

1. Confirm with user: "Built [ComponentName] with states: [list]. Missing from Figma: [list if any]. Registered in registry.ts."
2. If any tokens were unmapped or off-grid values rounded — summarize at the end.
3. Ask if a README was wanted or auto-generate it.
